{
 "_rule": "Finder scopes: three seats per dimension from round 10 (tvofi 2026-10-14), each a theme of its dimension's brief; D5 and D6 as many as their `ledger.max_units` needs, so each seat's text units are finishable (tvofi 2026-11-13). A seat is a list of blocks {files, steps, axis?}; files are globs over `git ls-tree -r --name-only <baseline>` (`*` stops at `/`, `**` crosses it) or the word \"rest\" (every universe file no seat of the dimension names explicitly for those steps). mode \"cells\": every (file, step, axis value) in universe x steps x axis is owned by exactly one seat. mode \"files\": every universe file by exactly one seat, every step by at least one. check_scopes.py enforces both and prints each seat's LOC; re-run it at the baseline, never carry its numbers.",
 "_pkg": "custom_components/heatpump_optimizer",
 "_coverage_excluded": {
  "_rule": "Tracked paths no dimension measures, each with its reason; check_scopes.py refuses a path in no universe and not here, an entry here that also names a covered path, and an entry that names nothing.",
  "dev/audit/rounds/**": "evidence records of past rounds (reports, verdicts, the harnesses findings ran): a finding re-measures one by its own harness, and a seat audits the mechanism, not the records it left (D11.md)",
  "dev/archive/**": "retired records and carries kept for history; no seat acts on them",
  "dev/programme/{delivery,register,round9,round10,triage}/**": "delivery rows, the register, round notes and triage records: records of decisions the mechanism already made",
  "docs/design/**": "dated design records of shipped features; the user docs D5 and D6 measure are what describes them now",
  "docs/site/fonts/**": "vendored font files and their SIL OFL licence texts; no behaviour and no claim",
  "tests/golden/**": "value-bearing golden fixtures, claimed and never re-derived by a finder (CLAUDE.md rule 3); the scripts that read them are in D3's and D11's universes",
  "tests/mutation_ledger/**": "recorded mutation outcomes and survivor triage; tests/mutation_table.py, which reads them, is measured",
  "{LICENSE,NOTICE}": "licence and attribution text; no behaviour and no claim a dimension can test"
 },
